<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mustēla</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mustella</span></b> , ae, f.
		mus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A weasel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">certum est mustelae posthac numquam credere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Stich. 3, 2, 43</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 4, 16, §
			60</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A fish;</i> acc. to some, <i>a
				lamprey;</i> acc. to others, <i>an eelpout</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				9, 17, 29, § 63</span></i>: marina, Enn. ap.
					<i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 299</span></i> (Heduph. v. 1
			Vahl.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
